  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive an array of **positive** integers `nums`.\n\nSneha and Rajesh are playing a game. In the game, Sneha can choose **either** all single-digit numbers or all double-digit numbers from `nums`, and the rest of the numbers are given to Rajesh. Sneha wins if the sum of her numbers is **strictly greater** than the sum of Rajesh's numbers.\n\nOutput `true` if Sneha can win this game, otherwise, output `false`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [1,2,3,4,10]\n\n**Output:** false\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nSneha cannot win by choosing either single-digit or double-digit numbers.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [1,2,3,4,5,14]\n\n**Output:** true\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nSneha can win by choosing single-digit numbers which have a sum equal to 15.\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [5,5,5,25]\n\n**Output:** true\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nSneha can win by choosing double-digit numbers which have a sum equal to 25.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 100`\n* `1 <= nums[i] <= 99`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
